# Secrets. The worker's real credentials live in `wrangler secret put`,
# never in the repo. These two files are the local-only mirror of that:
# `.dev.vars` is what `wrangler dev` reads, `.env` is the conventional
# name. Both carry a live key secret. Neither is ever committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example

# Wrangler's local state and anything npm leaves behind. There is no
# build step here and no package.json by design (see .claude/house-rules
# rule 2) — this is here so an incidental `npm i` cannot become a commit.
.wrangler/
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and OS litter.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
